 Note that a UE can always be provided with a switching pattern, but the application of the RRC configured switching pattern is specified in RAN4’s specification. So, the current description in RAN1 specification is not correct. Endorse TP#2 to TS 38.213 for alignment. Conclusions In this contribution, we express our views from both theoretical and practical perspectives and provide our proposal accordingly. The observations and the proposals are listed as follows. Observation 1: In addition to the antenna element placement affecting the polarization direction, the polarization direction also depends on the wire length connecting antenna element and oscillator. Observation 2: The maximum wire-length difference between antenna elements connecting to oscillator can exceed half a wavelength, and the polarization orientations of antennas at different locations vary substantially, showing fully randomized behavior across the measured frequency bands. Observation 3: UE implementation method is diverse among different vendors or companies, it would not be practical to use one model to cover different implementation specific variations. Proposal 1: To enhance the handheld antenna model, the parameters particularly related to polarization orientation should follow the actual measurement results of the real terminal products. Proposal 2: The polarization orientation issue in channel model should be addressed based on enough measurement results on the actual terminal product. Proposal 3: For periodic CSI-RS and semi-persistent CSI-RS on a serving cell configured in CSI report configuration in CSI-ReportConfig, The most recent CSI measurement occasion of semi-persistent CSI-RS resource or periodic CSI-RS resource on the serving cell occurs in the symbols available for

