 scheduling. In our view, difference between DCI for TCI state update and for SCell dormancy would stem only from the indicated functionality. Therefore, it would be a bit strange for us if RAN1 would take another direction for SCell dormancy indicating DCI from TCI state update DCI. One could indeed argue that such restriction on SLIV allowed for DCI for particular use cases may cause inflexible configurations. However, again, whether/how significant such inflexibility would be not very clear. Moreover, considering the agreement above, we think just to take an unified direction for similar functionalities would be implementation friendly. Given the above consideration, our view is as follows: Proposal 2: Adopt TP#1 for TS 38.213 for DCI format indicating SCell dormancy without scheduling PDSCH reception Reason for change: UE behavior for receiving SCell dormancy indication via DCI 1_1 when multi-PDSCH scheduling is configured is not clear Summary of change: Clarify that DCI format 1_1 including SCell dormancy indication indicates a TDRA row with only one SLIV entry Consequence if not approved: SCell dormancy may not work in FR2-2
